A||||14||loafer87gt||1FS2M6, what sort of motor are you running?||||1||
Z||000000||loafer87gt||11-06-2000||01:29 PM||||Just curious, are you running some sort of forced induction on your car? Twin-turbo? Is it a 2.8?||||reg||1
Z||000001||1FST2M6||11-06-2000||02:56 PM||||Currently i have according to Jeff (GT Bastard) Milled heads. I have in my posession 2 T-28 super 60 turbos and 1 TD-06sh. for either Bi-turbo or single turbo. either way i'll have a 25shot of nitrous (just because) and the turbo/s. I have an HKS Super Sequential Blow off valve and Turbonetics Delta gate purchased from Dynamic Turbo in Florida. The paint, Frame work and suspension wiped me out so the Haltech is on hold till i get my christmas bonus. Once i have all the parts assembled i'll drop it off at Engineered Performance <A HREF="http://www.engineered.net" TARGET=_blank>www.engineered.net</A>  for them to work their magic on. they did a GREAT job on my 86 SE. I have a Brullen 3" "Karbon" series it's just a carbon fiber packed muffler like a borla but not as loud. <A HREF="http://www.brullenexhaust.com" TARGET=_blank>www.brullenexhaust.com</A>   Also to come is water injection from <A HREF="http://www.f-max.com" TARGET=_blank>www.f-max.com</A>  i have an intercooler. provided by Custom Network Motors  <A HREF="http://cnmmotorsports.com/" TARGET=_blank>http://cnmmotorsports.com/</A>   builders of the worlds ONLY twin turbo CRX. (James {owner}) is a great guy and is a turbo GENIUS! I can get pics of everything lined up next to the car if ya like... not all that impressive but fun to play with. I will keep the motor as it sits. we were able to squeeze 13.6@103 in the 1/4 out of the old motor so it's a great platform to start from. and this one has low mileage to boot. and have spoken with Shaun41178 about tranny upgrades. he put me in touch with Pro-Torque. they make a stall converter for the TH125 for $395 I'll probly be picking that up too. i already have a shift kit. NGK plugs (UR5) MSD wires, and MSD blaster coil (for sale soon) and MSD 6BTM.  <P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/mouse.gif">   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/1fstsig1.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||1FST2M6||11-06-2000||03:03 PM||||before anyone gets huffy saying i'm braggin.. i'm not it's really on about $500 in parts (minus the intercooler and turbos which were donated) and i have to come up with about $2500 for the final fabrication and install||||reg||1
Z||000003||loafer87gt||11-06-2000||03:28 PM||||That 13.6 time you ran, was that with Jeff's normally aspirated v6? Just out of curiosity, how much would a place like engineered performance charge a customer to do a Twin-T install? During the summer my 2.8 threw a bearing and toasted the crank, so I'm looking for a good replacement motor. I talked to RSM, and I can get a built 3.0 motor for $3800 CDN, but that seems a little steep for 170 HP. I can get a brand new 3.4 Performance Crate engine for $2100 bucks, but GM will not offer any sort of warranty on the engine because it is going in a Fiero and because of the start hole modiification. I'm almost just thinking about taking my old 2.8 to a good shop to have it rebuilt. Once I get the car running, then I can drive it to a tuning shop to look at some turbocharging options. From your past experience with the Dyno, what sort of mods yielded the most bang for the buck. I've heard good things about aftermarket ignition systems and cat-back exhaust systems. Any advice on what route I should take with the car? ||||reg||1
Z||000004||1FST2M6||11-06-2000||03:58 PM||||if you just showed up at the door with nothing, about $4000 for custom kit including turbo and tuning. the BEST bang for the buck minus the nitrous was my 2.5" exhaust. the single in and single out aided in the scavaging effect/theory that was not just for looks but some sweet go too! i went with the 3" (on the current car) for obvious reasons (turbo.) the Crane HI-6s i had was ok but only yeilded about 6hp yanked it off and installed the MSD 6al and gained 4 more! the 13.6 was run wih a 40hp shot of nitrous. that was the best speed money i've ever spent. $400 for 2 full seconds off a factory car! just running the motor the SE would run 14.7. which is about a full second faster than a stock V6. K&N makes like 3hp-ish maybe.. i've got dyno results of that too. the throttle body was a nice upgrade but only made a difference with the nitrous running. (on the dyno and on the track) the Cross-flow mufflers that the camaro/firebird use back up a lot of gases and will create more back pressure. the single in single out will give you better HP and TQ numbers but your stuck with a single (functional) exhaust tip. which is fine with me.. i was going for function screw astetics! will be the same with the turbo installed on the GT. Headers are ok if your running high rpms all day if your a stop light racer save your money for gas and filling your nitrous bottle. porting the stock manifold was a great improvement as was wraping them with 1/8" header wrap (there was no measureable hp increase but it was cooler under the hood) the throttle body coolant bypass is free hp in cooler weather. but in EXTREME cases you can freeze your throttle body open (VERY unlikly in our cars due to it's placement right above the exhaust manifold y-pipe) uum lets see... Accel Super Coil was nice showed +.1HP  but it was an improvement. every little bit helps. Accel, MSD, Crane, taylor mallory all make good wires. magnecore. I'd shy away from Vitek. and any thing made by Python or Venom. (more smoke and mirrors than performance) I had RC injectors <A HREF="http://www.rceng.com" TARGET=_blank>www.rceng.com</A>  they are/were great but you get 10mpg. and have to burn a custom chip to make the car run worth a crap or at all. if you cut the cat off you get better sound but loose torque! a shift kit makes a nice drivability improvement. and the SE has an ACT 4 puck unsprung Clutch and ACT 2300# Pressure plate which is crappy for daily driving the better setup is a Beck Arnley Pressure plate and 4 puck unsprung hub disc. (plate available at NAPA <A HREF="http://www.napaonline.com" TARGET=_blank>www.napaonline.com</A>  ) and the cheaper ACT disc is available at <A HREF="http://www.clutchnet.com" TARGET=_blank>www.clutchnet.com</A>   you might want to check out Ed Parks place for a motor! a 3.6liter for pretty cheap with a warranty!!!  <A HREF="http://www.angelfire.com/biz/fierosails/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.angelfire.com/biz/fierosails/</A>   check out thier "fiero secrets" in engine area for his web page... <P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/mouse.gif">   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/1fstsig1.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000005||1FST2M6||11-06-2000||04:04 PM||||oh and jeffs car had a bad bearing that i replaced with +.001 rod bearings and yeah it still makes a bit of noise but still walks all over 3.1 fieros! with 2500+ miles on it and probly 5-6 dyno runs!    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> tuning makes a difference! I just hope this car responds as well as the 86 to modifications. I promised jeff i wouldn't change anything till i dynoed it as it sits... hope to do that this weekend...   <p>[This message has been edited by 1FST2M6 (edited 11-06-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000006||Shaun41178||11-06-2000||05:04 PM||||Best bang for the buck mods are as follows in my opinion.  <P>Ported TB.  Even though Travis said he only saw an improvement with nitrous I saw an improvement on my stock 2.8.  I picked up 4 peak hp and about 2-3 torque throughout the rpm band.  Dyno results are on my webpage for viewing.  I didn't test mine with nitrous.<P>Ported stock exhaust manifolds.  I picked up 8 peak hp on my internally stock 2.8.  I did lose about 5 lb-ft of torque around 2200 rpm though.  Oh yea I also provide ported stock exhaust manifolds for a reasonable price of $120.  hp gains should be around 6-10 hp improvement on a stock 2.8.  Email me for more details on the manifold porting.<P>2.5 catback exhaust.  Most muffler shops can make one for you.<P>Gutted cat.  Try to find a corner shop to do this as most big companies like Midas won't do it.<P>Underdrive pulley.  I picked up about 3 hp or so from this mod.  I saw a decrease in qtr mile times with this mod too of about .2 of a second.<P>Drop in K&N or a custom cold air intake system.  I picked up 2 hp from this mod but since have changed it around a bit to draw colder air.  I might have about 4 hp now from this mod.<P>Ignition system.  I didn't see any improvement with this mod on the dyno but I really only got it cause I had nitrous.<P>I think that is it as far as bolt on mods go without going internal.<P>I haven't really had any tuning on a dyno like Travis.  I just showed up there to compare bolt on power improvements.  My best time with these mods with my auto tranny is a 16.1 at 83 mph.  I have measured a best of 0-60 at 7.5 with my g-tech.  That is of course without my nitrous.  With nitrous I do it in a best of 5.6 with nothing slower then a 5.8<P>Oh and Travis, quit bragging as I am getting huffy and even a pit puffy.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Shaun-Toledo OH, 85 GT<BR>3.2 With nitrous<BR>http://members.aol.com/shaun41178||||reg||1
Z||000007||loafer87gt||11-06-2000||06:24 PM||||Thanks a lot for the info guys. So far I have allready done the ported manifolds, upgrade to Taylor 8.8 mm wires, and have the Holley scoop with a K & N filter. Where did you guys get your Throttle body boring work done at? I'm kinda stuck in a black hole as far as performance shops go.(middle of farmville Saskatchewan  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> ) If I was to go with the 3.4 or 3.6 conversion, would I need to upgrade to high flow injectors and buy a fuel pressure regulator? I know I would have to get my flywheel neutrally balanced as well, but this swap should be fairly straight forward and one of the local shops should be able to do it. Also, have you guys done any HP test for head porting?||||reg||1
Z||000008||GT Bastard||11-06-2000||07:43 PM||||That's right, those heads were milled .20, ported by my father, and and the valves were checked out along with new seals.  The manifolds were also ported.  All new gaskets in the top end.  Other than that, it's stock.<P>And yes, Trav did a helluva job on my SE with that combo...  Nobody can figure out why it's hauls ass so well with a dying 2.8 V6.  It should be even better yet with a fresh 3.2...  ||||reg||1
Z||000009||88formula||11-06-2000||08:07 PM||||1FST2M6, Can you tell me what you did to tune your SE v6 and what you did to the computer/prom if anything. I would really like to know.<P>Thanks<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000010||1FST2M6||11-07-2000||08:22 AM||||at WOT the TPS Trips a switch in the ECU that inturn makes the MSD run the ignition at nearly TDC. The RC injectors make a difference to. get plenty of fuel so that it NEVER leans out and wastes a piston. the intake air temp sensor has a capacitor wired in at the fire wall (under the head tape) to make the computer think it's 40* out side all the time since its on the firewall the heat from the exhaust warms it up and make it's resistance change a little so it doens't throw a code. the exhaust well we tried 3 different set ups... single in dual out ocelot (came on the car from previous owner)single in dual out (Flowmaster 50series) and the single in single out (40 series) the single in and single out made te best gains. I didn't do the under drive pulleys cause they don't seem to help other cars that had them at the shop... Shaun did see improvement (guess i should have bought them)the Fuel map has been changed also. I don't have the specifics of that.. i'll contact James at CNM and get them from him . He burned the chip to make the car run on the larger injectors. I'll go through my recipts and fing out what the resistance of the IAT cap is. more soon.. thanks for the the info Jeff... also had/have the fuel pump out of an 89 IROC-Z. and took the black plastic baffle out of the tank (at the base of the fuel pump. and stuck a nickel in the factory fuel pressure regulator. under the diaphram thei was good for another 5-10psi and only cost a nickel...  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><p>[This message has been edited by 1FST2M6 (edited 11-07-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000011||88formula||11-07-2000||04:58 PM||||So I think it was the custom computer chip that did the trick. The guy who made it for you must have got it just right.<P>Thanks.||||reg||1
Z||000012||1FST2M6||11-08-2000||10:45 AM||||james at custom network motors  <A HREF="http://cnmmotorsports.com" TARGET=_blank>http://cnmmotorsports.com</A>  he did the chip. <P>make it run..<BR>dyno it<BR>change it<BR>dyno it<BR>change it<BR>blah, blah, blah... all day one saturday!  James RULES!<p>[This message has been edited by 1FST2M6 (edited 11-08-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000013||88formula||11-08-2000||06:57 PM|||| I wish I had someone around here that could do that for me because I am building a high performance 3.4-liter engine that is similar to fierosounds 3.4-liter engine. How much did it cost you?||||reg||1
Z||000014||1FST2M6||11-09-2000||09:11 AM||||$200 for james' time and the 8 $3 E-Proms we trashed... Dyno time was free...||||reg||1
